git rebase -i HEAD~4  // where 4 is the number of changes including HEAD that you want to muck with

This will open up a prompt
// Btw change your preferred editor to emacsclient thus
git config --global core.edior emacsclient

Top of the prompt choose the first one as pick or edit message and apply squash to all others below it. This will
cause them to do hg qfold (or fold the commits into one)

Once you save and exit, it will open up another prompt with all the commit messages in place. Trim them in place and
save and you are in business!!

